Project Structure

Create a new folder alongside your backend.

Ecommerce-Devops-Project
│
├── backend
│
├── frontend
│
└── terraform

Go to your project root:

cd ~/Ecommerce-Devops-Project

Since we are building an interview-quality project, we'll use Vite instead of Create React App because it is the modern standard.

npm create vite@latest frontend -- --template react

Go to your project root:

$ cd ~/Ecommerce-Devops-Project
$ cd Ecommerce-app/
$ rm -rf frontend
$ npm create vite@latest frontend -- --template react

Go inside:

cd frontend

Install dependencies:

npm install

Install additional packages:

npm install axios react-router-dom
Why these?
axios → Call backend APIs
react-router-dom → Multi-page routing (Home, Cart, Orders, etc.)
Verify React

Start it:

npm run dev

Expected output:

Local:

http://localhost:5173

Open in browser:

http://localhost:5173

You should see the Vite React welcome page.

