Step (2): Configure Backend URL

$ nano api.js

import axios from "axios";

const api = axios.create({
  baseURL: "http://a7caabbdd3b17426498ad0863b24c192-1414738606.ap-southeast-2.elb.amazonaws.com",
});

export default api;


For now, replace <YOUR-ALB-DNS> with the DNS name of the ALB that exposes your backend.

Later we'll improve this by using environment variables (.env) so the URL isn't hardcoded.

